  "problem": "Consider the set $B=\\{1,2,3\\}$ and the relation $R=\\{(x,y)\\in {B}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y=3\\}.$\nFill in the missing values in the adjacency matrix of the relation:\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |\n| $2$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |\n| $3$ | $0$ | {{field-5}} | $0$ |",
